/P 179 0 R
/E (Going into the penultimate day, the Team was under the impression it would be smooth sailing. After they had cleared the Tilt Test and resolved majority of the points brought up during sound.  However, it was far from east. The team had to stay back in the Noise Bay and demonstrated relentless determination until they successfully addressed the inspector's concerns, finally passing the Noise Test.  Sometimes, a strategic timeout can make all the difference.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2 3]
>>
endobj
338 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 179 0 R
/E (Then came the Brakes Test, proving to be even more challenging due to a drained battery and an issue with a tyre refusing to lock up, among others. The team was fully committed to sorting every issue; multiple attempts were made using different drivers. However, the efforts went in vain because just when we had everything in place, the clock struck 6 PM. We were out of time, and today was the last day we could clear the tests to be eligible for the Dynamic Events. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4 5]
>>
endobj
